A||||3||yellowFormula||Engine, tranny help PLEASE
Z||000000||yellowFormula||06-22-99||10:45 AM||||I recently purchased a 88 Formula , pretty beat up with 122,000 miles. manual tranny, and I have some problems with it. <p>1.) You can switch gears without touching the clutch<br>2.) smoke on start up<br>3.) check engine light is on<br>4.) Shifting is rough<br>5.) emergency brake is not working<p>If your wondering why I bought it with all these problems was because the guy only wanted 500 for it and I couldnt refuse.  I figure if I cant fix it I'll part it out, because there are a lot of good parts still on it. <p> 	
Z||000001||theogre||06-22-99||11:51 AM||||startup smoke, blue, is usually shot valve stem seals. It's annoying to fix, but not difcult. on a v6 you need gaskets for the manifolds... you have to pull them to get the vavle covers off.<p>run a code check and see why the light is on. it only takes 10 minutes. If you get an ECM scanner you can check all the sensor functions really quick. (It's worth the 150$us. You'll use it every time the engine flips out.)<p>the e brake could be several things, all repairable. Pull the handle and watch what moves, or doesn't.<p>the Clutch..... now there's a giant pain in the head. That's likely going to cost you. Read the old clutch threads. there are a few.<p>Shifting w/o the clutch, I assume when you are moving, may mean either the trany has been altered, or the syncro's are screwy. messed up syncros can also cause hard shifting even if the clutch is perfect. The syncros are little brakes inside the tranny that make the speed of the couplers matchup just before you lock them in. It keeps you from banging the coupler teeth up, and making the "grinding gear" noise.
Z||000002||batboy||06-22-99||08:11 PM||||YellowFormula, if you have another non-88 Fiero, check out the front suspension assembly and see if the entire thing is interchangable. That would be a great way to upgrade an older Fiero. A 1988 parts car would be a plus in my book.<p>Ogre is right about blue smoke on start up probably means an oil problem. Which is very common on a tired engine. You didn't really say what color it was, though.<p>It's also possible that it could be a black sooty smoke too, if the car is running overly rich. If a computer sensor is bad, it could be causing the computer to do weird stuff. The check engine light is on, so you know something's not right.<p>A white smoke is sometimes caused by a coolant leak that's turned to steam (such as a cracked head). Good luck.
Z||000003||Bozone||06-23-99||12:13 PM||||yellowFormula - check that car out good. You have a rare one. An original yellow 88 Formula? there were only 436 made and I'm sure a lot of them are crunched by now. There was an 88GT T-top at a show I went to over the weekend and the guy was offered $20,000 for it. BUT... it had less than 6K miles and was showroom condition. Nonetheless you might want to think before you part it out. See what Ed Parks at Fiero Factory has to say.
